Independently verify the ThothOS companion security fix tracked as ThothOS W-1850.

The reviewer must inspect the committed host implementation and rerun its focused evidence:

- exactly one audience input at every workspace call site;
- the legacy goobs 0.302.5 viewer role is derived only inside the compatibility boundary;
- customer task projection omits raw comment IDs and staff fields;
- customer comment single/batch reads and mutation responses omit internal comments,
  visibility metadata, and edit history;
- customers cannot create the reserved internal marker or mutate an internalized comment;
- comment editing remains functional without raw comment IDs;
- focused tests, typecheck, lint, codegen check, sanctioned-crossing guard, and the exact-SHA
  ThothOS build receipt pass.

Primary ThothOS implementation commits include 7c950c09ce, 534175ce73, 733e9df0b7,
b148c1cad0, d4b4e8a4ba, and the contract commit be1bf7e20b. The final verification must
use the W-1850 closeout evidence and exact implementation SHA rather than trusting this list.
